BILL OF MATERIALS — F.R.I.D.A.Y.
==================================================

CORE COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------
Item                                Qty   Purpose
--------------------------------------------------
ESP32 DevKit V1 (30-pin)             3    Microcontroller — Base A, Drone, Base C
SX1262 LoRa Module (868 MHz)         4    Radio — 1 each for Base A/C, 2 for drone
LPDA Directional Antenna             1    Uplink leg: Base A to Drone
IPEX Omnidirectional Antenna         2    Downlink leg: Drone to Base C
N-to-SMA Adapter                     1    Connects LPDA to coax feed
SMA-to-U.FL Pigtail Cable            1    Connects adapter to radio module
AMS1117 3.3V Regulator Module        1    Drone power regulation (mandatory)
SW-420 Vibration Sensor Module       1    Hardware disaster-trigger demo


POWER & ASSEMBLY
--------------------------------------------------
Item                                Qty   Purpose
--------------------------------------------------
USB Power Bank (5V)                 2-3   Field power — Base A / Base C
Jumper Wires (assorted)             1 set General wiring
Breadboard or Perfboard              3    Circuit assembly per node
Micro-USB / USB-C Cables             3    Programming + power


NOTES
--------------------------------------------------
- Do not power two SX1262 radios from the ESP32's onboard
  3.3V rail alone. The external AMS1117 on the drone board
  is required to avoid brownout-induced radio resets.

- LPDA antennas are often rated near 12 dBi, but that is
  typically a peak figure at 3+ GHz. Budget link margin
  using a realistic 5-7 dBi at 868 MHz instead.

- RadioLib (by Jan Gromes) is required for the SX1262's
  BUSY, RXEN, TXEN, DIO1, and TCXO pins. The older Sandeep
  Mistry LoRa library does not support these.
